sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Kafka
    participant Orch as Orchestrator
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Provider as Proxmox Provider

    Kafka-)Orch: Deliver event E at generation 0 for instance I
    Orch->>DB: Insert unique receipt (consumer, E, 0) and admit workflow I
    Orch->>Provider: Execute provider step once
    Provider-->>Orch: Provider task reference and result
    Orch->>DB: Complete checkpoint, inbox receipt E, and result outbox
    Orch-->>Kafka: Commit consumed offset

    Kafka-)Orch: Redeliver event E at generation 0
    Orch->>DB: Insert unique receipt (consumer, E, 0)
    DB-->>Orch: Unique conflict identifies ordinary duplicate
    Orch->>DB: Read completed receipt and recorded outcome
    Orch->>Orch: Reuse recorded outcome and skip side effects
    Orch-->>Kafka: Commit duplicate offset

    Note over Kafka,Provider: Only governed replay can use generation n+1 and a broker duplicate cannot allocate it.
